5
00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:31.231
In this verse, Lord Krishna compares two

6
00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.231
types of karma yogis –

7
00:00:34.423 --> 00:00:37.423
those attached to results,

8
00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:40.846
and those who are free from desire for outcomes.

9
00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:44.615
While explaining the essence of previous verses,

10
00:00:44.654 --> 00:00:47.500
Lord Krishna also states that actions

11
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.808
done with true intention are indeed superior.

12
00:00:56.269 --> 00:00:58.462
Lord Krishna clarifies

13
00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:01.154
the difference between actions done with attachment,

14
00:01:01.154 --> 00:01:03.269
and those performed

15
00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:06.269
with detachment.

16
00:01:06.346 --> 00:01:08.115
Lord Krishna explains that

17
00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:09.538
the mindset we hold

18
00:01:09.538 --> 00:01:11.769
while performing actions

19
00:01:11.769 --> 00:01:15.077
directly impacts the results of those actions.

20
00:01:15.692 --> 00:01:18.231
One who acts without selfish desire,

21
00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:21.192
free from attachment to results,

22
00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:24.192
viewing work as sacred duty,

23
00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:27.269
attains true peace.

24
00:01:27.269 --> 00:01:29.423
This peace remains stable,

25
00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:32.500
undisturbed in any situation.

26
00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:35.154
This becomes possible because

27
00:01:35.154 --> 00:01:36.615
such a person

28
00:01:36.615 --> 00:01:38.385
offers the fruits of their actions

29
00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:40.654
to the Divine.

30
00:01:40.654 --> 00:01:42.192
The purpose behind

31
00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:44.231
such a person's actions is

32
00:01:44.231 --> 00:01:46.154
to follow the teachings

33
00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:49.154
given by the Lord.

34
00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:52.231
This is why Lord Krishna calls them "yukta."

35
00:01:52.462 --> 00:01:53.500
Meaning,

36
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.308
such a person

37
00:01:54.308 --> 00:01:57.308
becomes connected to God through devotion.

38
00:01:57.462 --> 00:01:58.577
On the other hand,

39
00:01:58.577 --> 00:01:59.885
one who has no interest

40
00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.231
in spiritual principles

41
00:02:02.231 --> 00:02:05.231
is called "ayukta" by Lord Krishna.

42
00:02:05.231 --> 00:02:06.769
This person's mindset,

43
00:02:06.769 --> 00:02:09.346
driven by selfish desires,

44
00:02:09.346 --> 00:02:10.846
seeks material gain

45
00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:14.077
and success behind every action.

46
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.500
Therefore, this person receives bondage

47
00:02:17.577 --> 00:02:19.654
instead of liberation.

48
00:02:19.654 --> 00:02:22.192
Lord Krishna's teaching here is well-suited

49
00:02:22.192 --> 00:02:25.192
to Arjuna's state of mind.

50
00:02:25.231 --> 00:02:26.385
Arjuna was troubled

51
00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:27.423
by concerns about fighting

52
00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:29.885
his loved ones

53
00:02:29.885 --> 00:02:32.885
and thus wanted to withdraw from battle.

54
00:02:33.077 --> 00:02:35.462
But here Lord Krishna explains that

55
00:02:35.462 --> 00:02:36.000
true peace

56
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.077
lies not in escaping duty,

57
00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:40.731
but in performing it with the right viewpoint –

58
00:02:40.731 --> 00:02:43.808
free from personal gain

59
00:02:43.808 --> 00:02:47.038
and aligned with divine will.

60
00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.846
A popular belief

61
00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:55.615
has become the foundation

62
00:02:55.615 --> 00:02:58.615
for most human lives –

63
00:02:59.462 --> 00:03:02.462
that life's main mantra is just

64
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.038
to indulge and remain absorbed

65
00:03:06.077 --> 00:03:09.077
in pleasures derived from them.

66
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.077
And if I tell you

67
00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:18.269
that this thinking mostly

68
00:03:18.577 --> 00:03:21.423
yields opposite results,

69
00:03:21.423 --> 00:03:24.769
would you believe it?

70
00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:27.769
Imagine a person

71
00:03:28.077 --> 00:03:31.077
constantly seeking more wealth, fame

72
00:03:31.115 --> 00:03:31.615
and comforts.

73
00:03:31.615 --> 00:03:34.615
They think that life's joy lies

74
00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.615
in acquiring

75
00:03:37.615 --> 00:03:39.846
all these things,

76
00:03:39.846 --> 00:03:42.846
and therefore

77
00:03:43.115 --> 00:03:46.115
that becomes their only goal.

78
00:03:46.654 --> 00:03:49.192
But what happens?

79
00:03:49.192 --> 00:03:52.192
As soon as one desire is fulfilled,

80
00:03:52.423 --> 00:03:56.615
a new desire is born with it.

81
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.038
And with that new desire come

82
00:04:01.038 --> 00:04:05.077
new worries and new problems.

83
00:04:06.808 --> 00:04:09.808
Understand this with an example –

84
00:04:10.462 --> 00:04:12.269
a small child

85
00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:15.385
tries to catch his own shadow,

86
00:04:16.577 --> 00:04:18.231
but

87
00:04:18.231 --> 00:04:21.231
does that shadow ever come into his hands?

88
00:04:21.385 --> 00:04:22.423
No, right!

89
00:04:22.423 --> 00:04:23.615
Similarly,

90
00:04:23.615 --> 00:04:26.615
one who keeps chasing pleasures

91
00:04:27.115 --> 00:04:30.000
finds joy and contentment remain

92
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
beyond their reach.

93
00:04:33.808 --> 00:04:36.346
And what do they get instead,

94
00:04:36.346 --> 00:04:39.346
joy or discontent?

95
00:04:39.769 --> 00:04:43.346
Now, consider another perspective.

96
00:04:43.846 --> 00:04:46.846
A person fulfilling their duties,

97
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.154
working hard,

98
00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:51.846
moving towards their goals,

99
00:04:51.846 --> 00:04:53.038
yet

100
00:04:53.038 --> 00:04:56.731
not attached to the results of their work.

101
00:04:57.615 --> 00:05:00.615
Instead, they surrender the fruits

102
00:05:01.231 --> 00:05:04.231
of their actions to God.

103
00:05:04.385 --> 00:05:07.231
Such a person also experiences joy

104
00:05:07.231 --> 00:05:09.385
but

105
00:05:09.385 --> 00:05:12.615
not in enjoying the results of their actions

106
00:05:13.538 --> 00:05:16.769
but in fulfilling their duty.

107
00:05:18.038 --> 00:05:19.731
This is what it means

108
00:05:19.731 --> 00:05:22.731
to act without

109
00:05:22.731 --> 00:05:25.269
attachment.

110
00:05:25.269 --> 00:05:29.308
The peace gained from this doesn't depend on life's ups and downs,

111
00:05:30.154 --> 00:05:31.423
because

112
00:05:31.423 --> 00:05:35.346
you rise above the endless cycle

113
00:05:36.423 --> 00:05:39.423
of desire and disappointment.

114
00:05:43.269 --> 00:05:45.269
Often in family life,

115
00:05:45.269 --> 00:05:48.308
each member wants everything

116
00:05:48.423 --> 00:05:51.692
done according to their own wishes.

117
00:05:52.077 --> 00:05:55.731
But this approach usually makes situations

118
00:05:56.308 --> 00:06:00.115
even more difficult and challenging.

119
00:06:02.038 --> 00:06:04.000
Imagine

120
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.615
there's a disagreement over something really small.

121
00:06:08.423 --> 00:06:11.846
Like how household chores should be managed

122
00:06:12.346 --> 00:06:15.885
or how children should be raised.

123
00:06:16.538 --> 00:06:17.308
Every member

124
00:06:17.308 --> 00:06:17.808
wants that task

125
00:06:17.808 --> 00:06:20.808
done according to their wishes.

126
00:06:21.615 --> 00:06:24.308
Then, what happens?

127
00:06:24.308 --> 00:06:27.308
The same story that plays out in every home.

128
00:06:28.231 --> 00:06:31.231
The situation deteriorates quickly.

129
00:06:31.346 --> 00:06:34.346
Each member in the family tries to push their preference

130
00:06:34.538 --> 00:06:36.192
and control

131
00:06:36.192 --> 00:06:39.192
the outcome.

132
00:06:40.308 --> 00:06:42.423
What was a small matter

133
00:06:42.423 --> 00:06:45.500
now becomes a cause for conflict, tension

134
00:06:45.769 --> 00:06:48.769
and unrest in the home.

135
00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:50.115
Now,

136
00:06:51.385 --> 00:06:54.192
consider a different perspective.

137
00:06:54.192 --> 00:06:57.192
Instead of forcing your view,

138
00:06:57.308 --> 00:07:00.385
what happens if you try to listen

139
00:07:00.692 --> 00:07:03.692
and understand others' opinions?

140
00:07:04.154 --> 00:07:06.154
Then what happens?

141
00:07:06.154 --> 00:07:08.577
Then there will be discussion of ideas,

142
00:07:08.577 --> 00:07:11.577
not disputes.

143
00:07:11.577 --> 00:07:12.769
Then everyone will try

144
00:07:12.769 --> 00:07:15.769
to find a solution

145
00:07:15.769 --> 00:07:18.769
rather than proving themselves right.

146
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.346
When you stop trying to control

147
00:07:21.346 --> 00:07:23.577
the situation to your liking

148
00:07:23.577 --> 00:07:25.846
and instead

149
00:07:25.846 --> 00:07:28.846
try to understand others

150
00:07:29.154 --> 00:07:32.154
and offer your support,

151
00:07:33.038 --> 00:07:34.731
solutions

152
00:07:34.731 --> 00:07:37.731
begin to emerge naturally.

153
00:07:38.385 --> 00:07:40.346
So always remember

154
00:07:40.346 --> 00:07:44.038
that family welfare comes

155
00:07:44.538 --> 00:07:47.538
not from mutual disagreement

156
00:07:47.577 --> 00:07:50.577
but from cooperation.

157
00:07:55.154 --> 00:07:57.692
When everyone's work in any workplace

158
00:07:57.692 --> 00:08:00.000
is driven by

159
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.000
personal interest,

160
00:08:03.038 --> 00:08:05.731
the entire organization's atmosphere

161
00:08:05.731 --> 00:08:06.346
is affected.

162
00:08:08.115 --> 00:08:09.038
When work is done putting self-interest first,

163
00:08:09.038 --> 00:08:12.769
an environment of competition,

164
00:08:13.731 --> 00:08:14.269
distrust,

165
00:08:14.269 --> 00:08:17.692
and negativity forms

166
00:08:18.038 --> 00:08:21.077
in that workplace.

167
00:08:21.615 --> 00:08:23.885
If an employee

168
00:08:23.885 --> 00:08:26.038
works for personal gain instead of the collective progress

169
00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.231
of their organization,

170
00:08:28.231 --> 00:08:31.731
how will they receive cooperation

171
00:08:31.731 --> 00:08:34.385
from their colleagues?

172
00:08:34.385 --> 00:08:36.538
It's possible that such selfish behavior

173
00:08:36.538 --> 00:08:39.731
may yield short-term benefits.

174
00:08:39.731 --> 00:08:42.885
But

175
00:08:44.038 --> 00:08:45.423
this negative mindset spreads rapidly

176
00:08:45.423 --> 00:08:49.077
in the workplace.

177
00:08:49.769 --> 00:08:52.731
And

178
00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:54.615
what is the result?

179
00:08:54.615 --> 00:08:56.577
People

180
00:08:56.577 --> 00:08:57.846
begin blaming each other

181
00:08:57.846 --> 00:09:00.846
and create such an atmosphere of mutual conflict

182
00:09:01.462 --> 00:09:03.885
where progress

183
00:09:03.885 --> 00:09:06.885
becomes impossible.

184
00:09:07.731 --> 00:09:10.731
However,

185
00:09:10.731 --> 00:09:13.000
there is a way to break

186
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.615
this negative cycle.

187
00:09:14.615 --> 00:09:17.615
If every member understands

188
00:09:17.846 --> 00:09:21.077
how personal interests can put the organization's work

189
00:09:22.038 --> 00:09:24.692
in great peril,

190
00:09:24.692 --> 00:09:27.692
they can think

191
00:09:29.077 --> 00:09:29.846
about the progress

192
00:09:29.846 --> 00:09:31.154
of the organization through their actions

193
00:09:31.154 --> 00:09:34.192
and work accordingly.

194
00:09:34.654 --> 00:09:37.654
And by doing so,

195
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.231
they can also free themselves from this negative cycle.

196
00:09:40.231 --> 00:09:43.538
And a positive environment filled with mutual contribution

197
00:09:44.115 --> 00:09:47.808
will form

198
00:09:48.269 --> 00:09:51.269
where everyone can flourish.

199
00:09:51.769 --> 00:09:54.769
Remember that an efficient organization

200
00:09:55.731 --> 00:09:59.038
moving toward its goal with truth

201
00:09:59.346 --> 00:10:02.346
cannot be stopped by anyone.